he same values. 🔴 **[F-1628-2 — READ THIS BEFORE YOUR NEXT GATE] `test:node-guards` PRODUCES FALSE REDS IN A SCRATCH GATE WORKTREE.** rc=1 with 5 failures in `gate-s1628` — but **slice REVERTED in the SAME root reproduces them identically**, and post-merge **from main’s root with the slice merged** both leaves are **rc=0** (`suite-red-inventory` 1.8 s, `fixture-teardown` 43.9 s). The reds track the **ROOT**, not the content: the test `scriptCopies()` the reducer to a temp dir, which a worktree whose `node_modules` is a symlink into main breaks. ⚠️ **UNEXPLAINED RESIDUE I will not smooth over: drain 1 ran the FULL battery in that SAME worktree at rc=0** — so it is not deterministic per-root; accumulated fixture state matters. **INTERIM LAW: re-run any such red from the main repo root before believing it.** The memory index records the inverse seam (scratch roots make tracked-subject guards *vacuous*); this is the **false-red** side, which costs more. 🔴 **[F-1628-3] SIX STALE ASSERTIONS IN A GAMEPLAY SUITE** — `m1-06` expects 5–6 `double_tap_coil` stacks against a cap of **3**, and an investment threshold of ≥22 returning 0. Control-confirmed on main. Its KNOWN-RED label is **13 days stale against a 7-day threshold with 353 commits since**, and membership is never exoneration (F-1444-2) — the control is what settled it. Fire-authorable corrective owed. 🛡️ **THE BASE MOVED MID-GATE AND §3.0b IS WHY IT COST NOTHING:** my first fast-forward was **REFUSED** — a concurrent Cowork agent committed `005753fc1` at 13:41 while playwright ran. Because the gate was detached, nothing was staged in main’s index: I reset to the new main, re-merged clean, verified `005753fc1` touched only `logs/` + `tasks/goals.json` (so it could not affect tsc/build/e2e), and landed. **The refusal is the cure working.** 🧾 **Duties:** GZ-01 **PAID** — the pick clock is player-visible, item *"The Draft Learns to Keep Time"* appended. TK-01 **not owed** (`ticker-digest-2026-08-09.md` covers yesterday).